      "writtenOn": "2020-01-21T21:27:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "how utilization is defined?is the info coming from app or framework? what if the information is wrong?\nI would rather let platform measure the load as the TA pgid package name is known, than let app give stuff like that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "fbd4c5b15e63a91dc1e0eb93e64cab6fa52b47f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d83ecc81_426f1d14",
        "filename": "power/aidl/android/hardware/power/IPower.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043625
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-21T22:39:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The info is coming from the app directly. The goal here is to allow the app to notify us before we actually could even theoretically measure a load change. Basically stuff like \"I just turned a corner and now I have twice as many entities to render. I haven\u0027t started rendering them yet, but you probably want to boost clocks so I don\u0027t drop the next frame.\"",
      "parentUuid": "ae6b80ef_cc0ba91e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 26
      },
